Repair the registered capability "bare-cedar-fog-free-compute-dev-activitypub" at lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/free-compute-dev (kind: systemd, entrypoint: src/serve-activitypub-face.mjs), which data/state/capability-registry.json reports BROKEN as of 2026-07-23. Registry error: crash-loops (auto-restart): ENOENT reading .../inference-work-lot-service/content/evm/accounts/eip155-31337.json -- a pnpm-hoisted dependency package is missing its content/evm/accounts fixture Health check to re-run once repaired: journalctl --user -u bare-cedar-fog-free-compute-dev-activitypub.service -n 20 Restore it to RUNNING_VERIFIED and update this entry's status in data/state/capability-registry.json accordingly.

---
Diagnosis from a prior hire:
1. Root cause: A pnpm-hoisted dependency package is missing its content/evm/accounts fixture file, specifically `.../inference-work-lot-service/content/evm/accounts/eip155-31337.json` (ENOENT error). This causes the systemd service to crash-loop with auto-restart enabled. The missing file is expected by the entrypoint at `src/serve-activitypub-face.mjs`.

2. Repair proposal: Re-install the pnpm-hoisted dependency package by running `pnpm install --force` from the project root at `lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/free-compute-dev`, then verify the file `inference-work-lot-service/content/evm/accounts/eip155-31337.json` exists in the node_modules directory. Restart the service with `systemctl --user restart bare-cedar-fog-free-compute-dev-activitypub.service` and confirm health with the specified journalctl command.

3. Unknown: The exact location of the pnpm-hoisted dependency package within the node_modules structure, and whether the missing file should be generated or restored from version control.

